Hints : $\int \frac{d x}{\sin x+\sqrt{3} \cos x}=\int \frac{d x}{2\left(\frac{1}{2} \sin x+\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \cos x\right)}=\frac{1}{2} \int \frac{d x}{\sin \left(x+\frac{\pi}{3}\right)}$
$$
\begin{aligned}
& =\frac{1}{2} \int \operatorname{cosec}\left(\mathrm{x}+\frac{\pi}{3}\right) \mathrm{dx}=\frac{1}{2} \log \left|\tan \left(\frac{\mathrm{x}}{2}+\frac{\pi}{6}\right)\right|+\mathrm{c} \\
& =\frac{1}{2} \ln \left|\tan \left(\frac{\mathrm{x}}{2}+\frac{\pi}{6}\right)\right|+\mathrm{c}
\end{aligned}
$$
